Asterium is a fork of Stellarium. The astronomy it computes is Stellarium's
work, so cite Stellarium for the science:

  Stellarium contributors (2026). Stellarium v26.2 Astronomy Software.
  URL https://stellarium.org/.
  DOI: 10.5281/zenodo.20835040

A BibTeX entry for LaTeX users is

.. code-block:: latex

  @Stellarium{,
    title = {{Stellarium} v26.2 Astronomy Software},
    author = {{Stellarium contributors}},
    year = {2026},
    url = {https://stellarium.org/},
    doi = {10.5281/zenodo.20835040},
  }

If what you are describing is this fork rather than the astronomy - its
interface, its packaging, or the data set it ships, which differs from
upstream's - say so alongside that citation and name it as Asterium, a modified
version of Stellarium. NOTICE.md lists what the modifications are. Asterium has
no DOI of its own and is not produced by or affiliated with the Stellarium
project; do not cite it as though it were Stellarium.
